{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units","id":854097,"title":"Thinking of replacing tribes with packs as werewolves primary social units","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-27T10:30:30-07:00","id":854097,"title":"Thinking of replacing tribes with packs as werewolves primary social units","content":"I've been creating a werewolf game and I've found I'd prefer to focus on the packs themselves and the interaction with other packs. None of the tribes really clicked with me. That added with a difficulty in understanding the circumstances on multi tribal pack led me to simply getting rid of tribes altogether.<br /> I'm pretty confidant on making things work together fluff wise but i need some help with the mechanic side of things.<br /> <br /> What should i do with:<br /> - The tribal renown<br /> Do i simply ignore the free point of renown usually awarded for tribes<br /> Or<br /> Do i make a sort of pack renown. Which could influence the interaction between packs.<br /> <br /> - The tribal gifts<br /> Do I let the players choose 3 gifts that could be associated with their pack totem<br /> Or<br /> Do i let the player choose 1 gift. With the possibility of getting more with exp expenditure (perhaps reflecting the pack totem getting other spirits allied that would teach gift of the chosen category)<br /> <br /> - The favored enemy (this is the crux of my problem with tribes as i much prefer the favored enemy to be at pack level and reflecting experience and recurring enemies within a pack territory)<br /> I'm thinking of having the favored enemy be a merit that a pack can buy with exp (a merit not unlike the fighting style format giving bonuses that would range from 1 to 5)<br /> First, the favored enemy chosen would have to be much more precise (ex: just beshilu instead of host).<br /> Also for the bonuses i'd see things like 9-again for rolls to determine if the favored enemy is involved here. Or free specialties in the favored enemy (perhaps letting players choose if the take the specialty on occult, investigation, intimidate, etc)<br /> I'd appreciate more help on constructing that merit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 03-27-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T10:54:48-07:00","id":854103,"title":"","content":"I would posit that packs are already the primary social units in Forsaken. Tribes are less like formal organizations and more like... Err... All of the werewolves that share a certain favored prey. If you've got a real hate-on for Shartha, you might ask your packmates if they know any special techniques for fighting them, and they'd direct you to the nearest allied Hunter in Darkness, who might be willing to teach you the tricks passed down from Black Wolf, if you're willing to accept Black Wolf's Ban.<br /> <br /> All that said, I don't want to come into a thread just to argue why you shouldn't hack the setting the way you want to hack it, so here's my advice on how to remove Tribe from Forsaken if you're of a mind to do so.<br /> <br /> What I would do is make Auspice as important to Uratha as Tribe is to the Pure. Give each Auspice a 4th Gift and two secondary Renown. Characters start with one dot in their Auspice's primary Renown, one dot in one of their Auspice's secondary Renown, and one dot in any Renown (can't raise any Renown to 3 at this point), two Facets from Gifts favored by their Auspice, a Moon Gift at dots equal to their Auspice primary Renown, and a Facet of a Wolf Gift if they only have one dot in their Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> As for Favored Prey, I would let individual characters pick theirs, so the pack isn't all stuck with the same Favored Prey. Maybe just pick one of the five and gain the Ban associated with that Prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:12:11-07:00","id":854108,"title":"","content":"You'd just run them like you would a pack of Ghost Wolves. No favored enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:15:40-07:00","id":854111,"title":"","content":"So, you have issues understanding why there would be multi-tribal packs in the setting? It boils down to having an expert on every front. Like Charlaquin said, packs already are the primary social unit in Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:22:56-07:00","id":854115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854103#post854103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would posit that packs are already the primary social units in Forsaken. Tribes are less like formal organizations and more like... Err... All of the werewolves that share a certain favored prey. If you've got a real hate-on for Shartha, you might ask your packmates if they know any special techniques for fighting them, and they'd direct you to the nearest allied Hunter in Darkness, who might be willing to teach you the tricks passed down from Black Wolf, if you're willing to accept Black Wolf's Ban.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree that Pack is definitely the primary social unit, but I think there is an argument to be made against Tribes. Especially if one wants to play up the territorial nature of wolfpacks, giving the PCs the ability to just run off and find another Hunter in Darkness pretty severely undermines territorial themes. Similarly if one wants to run without the sense of a global, unified Uratha community Tribes have basically got to go. All-in-all, though it's a bigger upfront investment by the storyteller, I think Packs and Lodges can provide everything Tribes do with more color and local flavor than tribes can offer (just look at Changeling, throwing away Seasonal Courts is, IMO, one of the best decisions of 2e). <hr />Anyway, to the topic at hand here's what I do:<br /> <br /> <b>Renown: </b>Packs get a Pack Renown, just as Tribes get a Tribal one. No noticeable mechanical changes required.<br /> <br /> <b>Gifts: </b>One favored Gift, associated with the Pack Totem. Lodges can provide another two, assuming that pack is okay with joining a regional coalition. Either way, just drop the exp differences between favored and unfavored Gifts, the hunting requirements for learning new Shadow Gifts are limit enough.<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Enemy</b>: I would have said just make it a pack thing, but I like your merit approach. I'll maybe put some thought to that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T11:31:42-07:00","id":854117,"title":"","content":"I get that but i still thinks that favored enemies are to vague as they are. I dont see the hunt for a beshilu being the same as for azlu. They have similarities sure but they would take much different strategies to spot that they are up to no good, to find them and to deal with them. And I really dont like the favored enemy spirits and humans as it could mean pretty much anything.<br /> Also i like the idea that a pack would have to go ask for knowledge or help from another pack.<br /> And yes i understand that pack are already the primary social unit for the Forsaken. I just didnt know what the proper title would be. Sorry.<br /> <br /> I understand that it would be best to have a member of each tribe to form the pack but i dont see how that happens organically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854103#post854103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I would do is make Auspice as important to Uratha as Tribe is to the Pure. Give each Auspice a 4th Gift and two secondary Renown. Characters start with one dot in their Auspice's primary Renown, one dot in one of their Auspice's secondary Renown, and one dot in any Renown (can't raise any Renown to 3 at this point), two Facets from Gifts favored by their Auspice, a Moon Gift at dots equal to their Auspice primary Renown, and a Facet of a Wolf Gift if they only have one dot in their Moon Gift.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea.<br /> <br /> For the favored enemy i'd want it to be something that develops out of an experience (having the beshilu wreck havoc in your territory for 5 years it would be pretty logical that the pack develops tactics and knowledge to deal with them no matter which 'tribe' intructed them first).<br /> I would also rule that the favored enemy could be taken multiple times.<br /> My goal here, i guess, is to have the pack develop how to deal with a threat gradually as its required.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I love the concepts of the firstborn. Its just the tribes I'm having trouble with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 03-27-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:12:52-07:00","id":854134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854117#post854117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that but i still thinks that favored enemies are to vague as they are. I dont see the hunt for a beshilu being the same as for azlu. They have similarities sure but they would take much different strategies to spot that they are up to no good, to find them and to deal with them. And I really dont like the favored enemy spirits and humans as it could mean pretty much anything.<br /> Also i like the idea that a pack would have to go ask for knowledge or help from another pack.<br /> And yes i understand that pack are already the primary social unit for the Forsaken. I just didnt know what the proper title would be. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. The only reason I recommended sticking with the five default ones is because that's what the Siskur Dah benefits all revolve around. But that might still be hackable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854117#post854117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that it would be best to have a member of each tribe to form the pack but i dont see how that happens organically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish I could offer more insight on this, but I'm so far on the opposite perspective that I can't see how it <i>wouldnt</i> happen organically. What is the barrier you're thinking would prevent this? Cause to me, it just seems totally natural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854117#post854117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, glad to know my advice helped!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854117#post854117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the favored enemy i'd want it to be something that develops out of an experience (having the beshilu wreck havoc in your territory for 5 years it would be pretty logical that the pack develops tactics and knowledge to deal with them no matter which 'tribe' intructed them first).<br /> I would also rule that the favored enemy could be taken multiple times.<br /> My goal here, i guess, is to have the pack develop how to deal with a threat gradually as its required.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. I could see it being a Merit kind of like Professional Training. You pick a specific type of enemy like &quot;Firetouched&quot; or &quot;Azlu&quot; or &quot;Death Spirits&quot; and each dot gives you some bonuses that apply to fighting that specific enemy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854117#post854117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be clear, I love the concepts of the firstborn. Its just the tribes I'm having trouble with.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, I would definitely recommend making the five Siskur Dah benefits Merits, with the drawback that you also gain the associated Firstborn's Ban.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, maybe your Professional Training-style Favored Prey Merit could start specific and get more broad at higher dots. Then the Siskur-Dah bonuses against the five default Favored Preu could be the fifth dot benefit of the Favored Prey Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:52:26-07:00","id":854162,"title":"","content":"Okay, i'll try to simulate the progression from first change to induction into a tribe.<br /> The way i see it when you get the first change IF you are already in a packs territory they find you and starts instructing you on the very basics (yes werewolves are real, dont eat human and the other tenets of the moon).<br /> After that the pack decides if they want another member in their pack. (werewolf lives being ... interesting, more often than not its the case) then they instruct the cub further. If they dont want the new werewolf in the pack (for whatever reasons, too many member, the new one doesnt match what the pack consider werewolfy enough, etc). Then they ask (sometimes agressively) to leave their territory. <br /> So, i expect thats the standard procedure. If your not to have the new werewolf you dont waste ressources training him. (maybe i see the packs as too selfish :P).<br /> I could see a meeting of the packs where you could shop for a tribe in a meeting of the pack ( i dont see just meeting of a particular tribe where one member in every pack leaves the territory for a reunion happening). There you have access to the different tribe that could induct you? <br /> <br /> Now i see that working (thats never been my problem) but i get the feeling it adds another 'group' to belong to when you just need the auspice as the spiritual identity and the pack as the physical identity (keeping with the duality themes)<br /> <br /> Arrgh. Sorry it all makes sense in my head but i cant express it very well X( .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T13:50:06-07:00","id":854194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854162#post854162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, i'll try to simulate the progression from first change to induction into a tribe.<br /> The way i see it when you get the first change IF you are already in a packs territory they find you and starts instructing you on the very basics (yes werewolves are real, dont eat human and the other tenets of the moon).<br /> After that the pack decides if they want another member in their pack. (werewolf lives being ... interesting, more often than not its the case) then they instruct the cub further. If they dont want the new werewolf in the pack (for whatever reasons, too many member, the new one doesnt match what the pack consider werewolfy enough, etc). Then they ask (sometimes agressively) to leave their territory. <br /> So, i expect thats the standard procedure. If your not to have the new werewolf you dont waste ressources training him. (maybe i see the packs as too selfish :P).<br /> I could see a meeting of the packs where you could shop for a tribe in a meeting of the pack ( i dont see just meeting of a particular tribe where one member in every pack leaves the territory for a reunion happening). There you have access to the different tribe that could induct you? <br /> <br /> Now i see that working (thats never been my problem) but i get the feeling it adds another 'group' to belong to when you just need the auspice as the spiritual identity and the pack as the physical identity (keeping with the duality themes)<br /> <br /> Arrgh. Sorry it all makes sense in my head but i cant express it very well X( .</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like your understanding is pretty much the same as mine. If it helps, try thinking about the tribe less as another group to belong to and more as a spiritual and martial tradition. Once you've taught the new cub the basics, it's time for the advanced classes, which includes the Tribes' special techniques for fighting specific enemies. So, if, for example, your First Change happened when your possessed father tried to kill you, once you've learned the basics of the hunt, you might want to delve more into how to fight possessed and Claimed. Your more experienced pack members might introduce you to the local Claimed expert, a disciple of Winter Wolf, who offers to teach you Winter Wolf's ways. This expert might be a member of the pack, or a member of an allied pack. Either way, if the pack didn't have a Storm Lord before, they will once you complete your training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T23:11:10-07:00","id":854370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854162#post854162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now i see that working (thats never been my problem) but i get the feeling it adds another 'group' to belong to when you just need the auspice as the spiritual identity and the pack as the physical identity (keeping with the duality themes)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to point out that there's no <i>requirement</i> for this. Sure, the most straightforward explanation is that you encountered someone who explained it and it was very convincing, but it's also entirely sensible to say that you had to deal with lots of Beshilu, became convinced of your territory's sacredness, learned how to shape your territory to become death traps for anyone who came in, especially the goddamn rats who scurry away so fast when you kick their asses, and simply picked up a dot of Cunning and a few Gifts in Warding as part of your backstory... all without ever meeting another Hunter.<br /> <br /> ...also, I flinch every time you guys use the term &quot;favored enemy&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T02:27:08-07:00","id":854396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854370#post854370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to point out that there's no <i>requirement</i> for this. Sure, the most straightforward explanation is that you encountered someone who explained it and it was very convincing, but it's also entirely sensible to say that you had to deal with lots of Beshilu, became convinced of your territory's sacredness, learned how to shape your territory to become death traps for anyone who came in, especially the goddamn rats who scurry away so fast when you kick their asses, and simply picked up a dot of Cunning and a few Gifts in Warding as part of your backstory... all without ever meeting another Hunter.<br /> <br /> ...also, I flinch every time you guys use the term &quot;favored enemy&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I use &quot;Sacred Prey&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T06:58:32-07:00","id":854455,"title":"","content":"I think, i understand things better now. The Sacred Prey is more of a philosophical/spiritual preference rather than their most favorite thing to kill.<br /> That being said i still dont like the choices made for the sacred prey of the tribes and would like concept closer to what they have for the pure.<br /> For exemple, the predator kings hunt those who fail to honor the hunt. Its less about a particular type of creature and more about a statement for what the tribes stands for.<br /> the way i see it, the tribes would have<br /> Blood Talons - Warriors<br /> Bone Shadows - Secrets<br /> Hunters in Darkness - Intruders<br /> Iron Masters - (honestly no idea what to put there)<br /> Storm Lords - The Weak<br /> <br /> That way i could still have a favored prey at the pack level that is more about experience with what you have in your territory and you'd have the philosophical teachings of the tribe as to what to look for in a Sacred Prey. <br /> By that i mean for exemple that with choosing warriors as their sacred prey, it exemplify the martial mindset of what the goal of the hunt means for the Blood Talons. It would still means that werewolves are considered good prey because their warriors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T07:34:34-07:00","id":854467,"title":"","content":"Since the Iron Masters are about change and civilization, conservatives, traditionalists, the unchanging or static.<br /> <br /> It's worth keeping in mind that the Pure sacred prey reflect the Pure, who are far more open and, occasionally, hypocritical in who is a worthy prey. It also allows for a lot more in-fighting, as you can just say your alpha isn't respecting the Hisil enough or isn't respecting his family enough and take him out. Opening that up to the Forsaken is probably going to lead to a lot more in-fighting among packs, especially without tribes as a social anchor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T12:30:42-07:00","id":854598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=854467#post854467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Iron Masters are about change and civilization, conservatives, traditionalists, the unchanging or static.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Ooh thats a great idea, i really like it.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:26:24-07:00","id":855239,"title":"","content":"I tend to regard tribes as orders of initiation, rather than meaningful social units. A tribe, as I'd run it, is the lineage of who found you and initiated you into the People. Sometimes you get a choice, sometimes you don't. Still, you get the benefit of your Firstborn's lore and alliances so long as you honor your vows, which is a powerful currency to carry you past your initiation. <br /> <br /> Multi-tribal packs seem like the most sensible route to me, because it means fewer vulnerabilities. A pack without a Bone Shadow can barely hunt spirits, while a pack with no Iron Master has to tread carefully around urban prey.<br /> <br /> However, for a pack-based splat replacement, i would probably retool the krewe mechanics of Geist. I never really liked WtF 1e's take on tribes, and was always looking at ways of adapting that system to replace it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:39:40-07:00","id":855252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=855239#post855239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pack without a Bone Shadow can barely hunt spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>They might have a bit of trouble with ghosts, but no werewolf pack would <i>ever </i>find itself &quot;barely able&quot; to hunt spirits. You might as well just pack up and go home if that happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:06:00-07:00","id":855276,"title":"","content":"A pack without a Boneshadow (or Barghest/Predator's Claim), or an Ithaeur, or any rites geared toward dealing with Spirits (Bottle Spirit, Twilight Purge, Banish, Shadowbind and Shadow Call) or any fetishes geared toward Spirit combat (i.e Whisper Knife), can barely hunt spirits, though, you have to admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:11:07-07:00","id":855279,"title":"","content":"At low rank, yes, I suppose they're somewhat limited in the material realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T15:15:58-07:00","id":855284,"title":"","content":"Right, of course. In the Shadow they still are pretty able to hunt as well as they hunt anything. But definitely in the physical realm and twilight, like the guys said, its pretty difficult. So he definitely has a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:20:16-07:00","id":855933,"title":"","content":"Yeah i never liked that the bone shadows were 'the spirit tribe'. I'd much rather up their connections with ghosts, death and the dead instead of spirits. After all there are ithaeur in every tribes.<br /> <br /> What i'm likely to do is i'll keep the tribes, but instead of being something that you join at the start, they will be there for the players who proves themselves in the eyes of the Firstborn spirits. ( i am aware that will make them more akin to lodges). Joining them will give the bonuses for the tribes sacred prey siskur-dah as well as a support network both with other werewolves and spirits.<br /> <br /> That works well for me since the story will start at very low level. My players will all have done goofed someway or another and thus have no choice (they could go solo but what kind of game would that be :P) but to form a pack from scratch with each other. Its a lazy/easy way to have character who doesnt necessarily know each other form a pack and claim an empty territory. They will be forced to take a very crappy territory. The game itself will start with the characters having found a small locus (it will be protected by maybe a cult of murderhobo or something). Next will follow a few 'clean the territory episodes'. I want there to be a nearby pack that will state it very clear that as soon as the territory is worth something they will try and take it from the players. Maybe after all of that, if the characters have shown inclination towards one tribe or another there will be a possibilty of initiation.<br /> <br /> Does that all work? It will be my first game of Forsaken and none of my players have ever played either so i just want to make sure it all make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:47:00-07:00","id":855962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=855933#post855933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah i never liked that the bone shadows were 'the spirit tribe'. I'd much rather up their connections with ghosts, death and the dead instead of spirits. After all there are ithaeur in every tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could add a new Tribe that is focused on the dead. There's a hint of one in the Eaters of the Dead lodge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That works well for me since the story will start at very low level. My players will all have done goofed someway or another and thus have no choice (they could go solo but what kind of game would that be :P) but to form a pack from scratch with each other. Its a lazy/easy way to have character who doesnt necessarily know each other form a pack and claim an empty territory. They will be forced to take a very crappy territory. The game itself will start with the characters having found a small locus (it will be protected by maybe a cult of murderhobo or something). Next will follow a few 'clean the territory episodes'. I want there to be a nearby pack that will state it very clear that as soon as the territory is worth something they will try and take it from the players. Maybe after all of that, if the characters have shown inclination towards one tribe or another there will be a possibilty of initiation.<br /> <br /> Does that all work? It will be my first game of Forsaken and none of my players have ever played either so i just want to make sure it all make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be an inclination to believe that all territory is claimed by werewolves, so new werewolves have to get small patches of land. I'm not saying that's you, I have no idea of knowing, it just happens a lot. This can justify them not having a locus at the start, or a very weak one, which is nice. But you can just go the other way, the players have no, or just a little nearby competition. The problem becomes finding new loci, which are probably claimed by spirits or other beings, like your cult or a skinchanger, or a coterie of vampires.<br /> <br /> In short, I'd suggest not giving crappy territory so much as untamed.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yes it's sound. You might want to start with a Siskur Dah. Werewolves, even straight out of character generation, are not feeble combatants, and seeing what they can do can save you a lot of time preparing challenges that are easily overcome. New to the game, it might take a while to get used to what is a challenge to the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:40:21-07:00","id":856018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=855933#post855933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i'm likely to do is i'll keep the tribes, but instead of being something that you join at the start, they will be there for the players who proves themselves in the eyes of the Firstborn spirits. ( i am aware that will make them more akin to lodges). Joining them will give the bonuses for the tribes sacred prey siskur-dah as well as a support network both with other werewolves and spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's how it works now. It's just that starting characters in Werewolf aren't fresh off the First Change, they've been at it at least long enough to earn 3 dots of Renown, learn First Tongue, get a Totem (or form a bond with their pack's preexisting totem), learn some Rites, and drop their Harmony from 9 to 7. Proving yourself to your Tribe and their Firstborn is something that could have happened in the character's background if the player so chooses. (By default, anyway. Obviously if you prefer to always play out Tribal initiations in-game, that's a legit call to make.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/854097-thinking-of-replacing-tribes-with-packs-as-werewolves-primary-social-units?p=855933#post855933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That works well for me since the story will start at very low level. My players will all have done goofed someway or another and thus have no choice (they could go solo but what kind of game would that be :P) but to form a pack from scratch with each other. Its a lazy/easy way to have character who doesnt necessarily know each other form a pack and claim an empty territory. They will be forced to take a very crappy territory. The game itself will start with the characters having found a small locus (it will be protected by maybe a cult of murderhobo or something). Next will follow a few 'clean the territory episodes'. I want there to be a nearby pack that will state it very clear that as soon as the territory is worth something they will try and take it from the players. Maybe after all of that, if the characters have shown inclination towards one tribe or another there will be a possibilty of initiation.<br /> <br /> Does that all work? It will be my first game of Forsaken and none of my players have ever played either so i just want to make sure it all make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It all sounds pretty good to me. I would recommend, if you're thinking about starting the characters very early on, to start out with less than the full starting Uratha template and add those benefits for free as they are earned in-game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}